# Reverse proxy fronting cubicle-web + cubicle-api behind one address.
#
# - Set CADDY_DOMAIN to a real hostname (a Cloudflare Tunnel hostname, your
#   VPS's domain, or a Tailscale MagicDNS name) and Caddy issues/renews a
#   real TLS cert automatically. Leave it unset for plain HTTP on :80 — fine
#   if you're only reachable over a Tailscale tailnet, since that traffic is
#   already end-to-end WireGuard-encrypted regardless of what's on top.
# - Route selection: everything under one of the backend's known route
#   prefixes goes to cubicle-api; everything else (the Next.js app, static
#   assets) goes to cubicle-web. The API has no `/api` prefix of its own
#   today, so this lists its routers explicitly instead.

{$CADDY_DOMAIN::80} {
	@api path /health* /auth* /devices* /agents* /tasks* /chat* /settings* /engines* /socket.io*
	reverse_proxy @api cubicle-api:8000

	reverse_proxy cubicle-web:3000
}
